cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Unfitted.jl in academic work, please cite the method paper
  under "preferred-citation" below. The other metadata describes the
  software itself.
title: Unfitted.jl
abstract: >-
  A compact, dimension-generic Julia implementation of unfitted
  multi-level hp refinement on axis-aligned Cartesian grids, with
  selective per-cell activation and finite-cell-method (FCM)
  immersed-boundary integration via non-negative moment-fit quadrature.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/schmaeke/Unfitted.jl
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - hp refinement
  - unfitted finite elements
  - multi-level hp
  - finite cell method
  - immersed boundary
  - julia
authors:
  - family-names: Schmäke
    given-names: Jan Niklas
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: Unfitted multi-level hp refinement on Cartesian grids
  authors:
